<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan de Oñate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1550–1626</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onati">Oñate</a> was a conquistador born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> who led settlers, soldiers and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Franciscans</a> up the Camino Real in 1598 and founded the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-fe-de-nuevo-mexico">Santa Fe de Nuevo México</a>. He became its first governor, but his brutal punishment of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acoma-pueblo">Acoma Pueblo</a> in 1599 and costly failures led to his recall. He was later convicted of mistreating colonists and natives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-de-onate.jpg" alt="Juan de Oñate" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A d v a n c e d S o u r c e P r o d u c t i o n s Advanced Source Productions · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Equestrian_statue_of_Juan_de_O%C3%B1ate.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
